  "question": {
    "text": "If $D=\\left|\\begin{array}{ccc}1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1+x & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1+y\\end{array}\\right|$ for $x \\neq 0, y \\neq 0$ then $D$ is"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "\ndivisible by neither $x$ nor $y$\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\ndivisible by both $x$ and $y$\n",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "\ndivisible by $x$ but not $y$\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\ndivisible by $y$ but not $x$",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "$D=\\left|\\begin{array}{ccc}1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1+x & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1+y\\end{array}\\right|$\n$\\mathrm{C}_2 \\rightarrow \\mathrm{C}_2-\\mathrm{C}_1$ \\& $\\mathrm{C}_3 \\rightarrow \\mathrm{C}_3-\\mathrm{C}_1$\n$\\left|\\begin{array}{lll}\n1 & 0 & 0 \\\\\n1 & x & 0 \\\\\n1 & 0 & y\n\\end{array}\\right|=x y$.\nHence $D$ is divisible by both $x$ and $y$."
  }
}